WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
Hannah: What if an invalid index remains? Cancellation doesn't always remove its entry.

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:14.137
Raj: We inspect index validity after failure. Then review cleanup as separate work.

3
00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:20.905
Anika: No invalid index exists tonight though. Our completed index passed all checks.

4
00:00:20.905 --> 00:00:27.890
Priya: Just to confirm, switch rollback first, right? That's the quickest temporary workaround.

5
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:34.610
Lukas: Yes, but it doesn't remove maintenance costs. Dropping needs its own reviewed procedure.

6
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:42.530
Raj: For this leaf, concurrent drop is supported. Outside transaction blocks, with dependencies checked.

7
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:50.043
Hannah: Don't generalize that to parent indexes. Engine and object restrictions still apply.

8
00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:56.883
Priya: Okay, let's keep it under observation. Maybe write costs emerge with tomorrow's peak.

9
00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:04.348
Lukas: The rollback trigger covers peak write delays. Removal requires approval, not automatic deletion.

10
00:01:04.348 --> 00:01:11.260
Anika: So, I'll keep both paths documented. Query rollback and index removal stay separate.

